# __NAME__ — on Replit

Generated by the mod protocol's `replit` module from `__MODULE__`.

`main.py` serves this module the way `m serve` does, so the Repl answers the
protocol's shape as soon as it is running:

| Request | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `POST /{fn}` | call a function, JSON body = kwargs, response `{"result": …}` |
| `POST /mod/__NAME__` | null call → module info (name, functions) |
| `GET /health` | liveness, plus the import error if the module did not load |
| `GET /` | info as JSON |

## Run it

1. Push this folder to a GitHub repo.
2. Open `https://replit.com/github/{owner}/{repo}` — Replit imports it.
3. Press Run. Deploy for a URL that does not sleep.
4. Back in the fleet:
   `m replit/link __NAME__ https://<your-repl>.replit.dev`
   then `m replit/call __NAME__ info`.

